  "limitations": [
    "IPS solver/collector, aligned multi-rate physical schedule, compact metadata/tickets and improved RF capture are proposed, not deployed or hardware qualified.",
    "Existing relative PPS results do not establish pseudorange noise, anchor differential RF timing, calibrated UTC, GNSS equivalence or position accuracy. All cited denominators and tails retain their separate scope.",
    "Finer counters only improve quantization; fixed detector delay, multipath, clock transfer, correlation, geometry and motion can dominate.",
    "Clock-map discipline does not align physical advertising timers or establish RF carrier coherence. Multi-train capacity, scheduler phase control, actual channel switching and airtime require exact-target validation.",
    "Scheduled time-separated observations are the baseline. Same-channel overlapping BLE packets are not GNSS-like orthogonal signals. True multiuser waveforms/baseband require additional hardware/protocol capability.",
    "Toy noise, bias, static averaging, survey, quantization and scheduling assumptions are analytical sensitivity examples, not measured positioning or cost savings.",
    "Billion-scale shipment context is not an installed or compatible MCU count. No all-MCU firmware upgrade path is established.",
    "External review includes primary documentation and limited ESA search extractions; no full literature or normative standards conformance audit."
  ],
